## Annual premium

chart bar plans x=plan y=annual premium unit=$ labels focus="Premier" title="Annual employee premium"

## Who each plan suits

- **Basic:** the lowest premium at 168 dollars a year, with the lowest annual maximum and the highest deductible. No orthodontia.
- **Plus:** a higher annual maximum of 1500 dollars and a lower deductible of 50 dollars. No orthodontia.
- **Premier:** employees who want orthodontia cover, at 50 percent up to a lifetime maximum of 1500 dollars, for 492 dollars a year.
- **Family Max:** families with ongoing orthodontia. It has no deductible and a 2000 dollar lifetime orthodontia maximum.

## Recommendation

Make Premier the default plan. It is the lowest-cost plan with orthodontia cover, which matters because 38 employees said they have children who will need braces soon.

Family Max costs 264 dollars more a year than Premier and only pays off for families with ongoing orthodontia.
